{
  "about": "The second shared terrain fixture (SPEC section 8, the terrain grid; brief M2-02, review finding M1-R1-T-02; its pipeline half in brief M2-01). tests/shared/terrain_fixture_nw/ holds a synthetic world (world.json: origin E 2700000 / N 1100000, height_offset_m -12.25, the owner's axes), its terrain (2 m) and datasets configs, a synthetic 0.5 m source (source.f32) and the expected pipeline output under generated/ (manifest.json, terrain/fixture_nw.json, terrain/fixture_nw.f32), computed by design two independent ways (an exact rational area-weighted mean and the 64-bit window rule; identical bits). Unlike the first fixture it lies north-west of its origin (local x -1036 to -1012, z -1034 to -1008), at 2 m, and crosses x = -1024 and z = -1024, so it spans the four 1024 m Terrain3D regions (-2, -2), (-1, -2), (-2, -1) and (-1, -1). The pipeline must reproduce generated/ byte for byte; the game must load it into Terrain3D and read these heights back. Heights are local y = H - height_offset_m, float32; every y below is exactly representable in 32 bits.",
